<BaseLayout title="About Poorbita"><section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">About Poorbita</p><h1>Rooted here.<br>Growing together.</h1><p>For more than two decades, Poorbita has worked to strengthen rural livelihoods and protect the cultural knowledge that makes communities distinctive.</p></div></section><section class="section"><div class="container story"><div><p class="eyebrow">Our story</p><h2>Development with dignity.</h2></div><div><p>Poorbita is an initiative of Egra Agriculture and Rural Development Society, registered in 2005–2006. It began with a clear purpose: to improve livelihood opportunities for rural communities in West Bengal through agriculture, horticulture, pisciculture and handicrafts.</p><p>That purpose has grown into skills training, design development, farmer support, market connections, cultural programs and community care—all shaped around independence rather than dependency.</p></div></div></section><section class="vision"><img src="/images/about.jpg" alt="Community members at a Poorbita program"><div><p class="eyebrow">Our vision</p><h2>A future shaped by the people who live it.</h2><p>We envision rural and tribal communities with the skills, resources and partnerships to improve their income and quality of life—while keeping India’s rich tribal arts and cultural heritage alive.</p></div></section><section class="section values"><div class="container"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">How we work</p><h2>Principles that keep us grounded.</h2></div></div><div class="cards"><article><span>01</span><h3>Community first</h3><p>We begin with local realities, knowledge and aspirations.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Skills that endure</h3><p>We focus on practical capability and sustainable livelihoods.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>Culture with value</h3><p>We treat heritage as identity, knowledge and economic opportunity.</p></article></div></div></section></BaseLayout>
<style>.story{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:100px}.story>div:last-child{font:400 1.3rem/1.6 var(--serif)}.story p+p{margin-top:25px}.vision{background:var(--green);color:#fff;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.vision img{height:620px;object-fit:cover}.vision>div{padding:100px clamp(35px,8vw,120px);display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center}.vision .eyebrow{color:var(--gold)}.vision p:last-child{margin-top:28px;color:#d0dcd8}.values{background:var(--cream)}.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:1px;background:var(--line)}.cards article{padding:42px;background:var(--cream);min-height:250px}.cards span{font-size:.75rem;color:var(--rust)}.cards h3{margin:35px 0 18px}.cards p{color:var(--muted)}@media(max-width:760px){.story,.vision,.cards{grid-template-columns:1fr}.story{gap:30px}.vision img{height:430px}.vision>div{padding:70px 25px}}</style>
